**Judy Brutz** (Judith L. Brutz, 1940-2023, she/her) was a pioneer in researching Quaker family violence which led a
lifelong public ministry. Judy Brutz held dual monthly meeting membership in Cleveland Meeting (Lake Erie Yearly Meeting
and Ohio Conservative) and Des Moines First Friends Church (Iowa FUM). As an educator and therapist, she founded the
Friends Family Service of Iowa Yearly Meeting. 

In remembrance, Friend Joan Liversidge wrote “[Honoring an Elder in Our
Work Against Interpersonal Violence: A Friend’s Recollection of Judy Brutz](/reference/judy-brutz/honoring-an-elder)”


Her [initial 1984 research]({{baseurl}}/reference/judy-brutz/1984-conflict-resolution-in-quaker-families) compared a national study on family violence with responses from Quakers (130 males and 158
females). In general, there were no significant differences, though differences were found in patterns of violence.

In her later life she wrote many spiritual books including biblical exploration and poetry. She wrote much original
poetry using form and themes from the Lord’s Prayer.


